ective study of coronary heart disease. <source>Fed Proc</source><year>1962</year>;<volume>21</volume>:<fpage>52</fpage>-7.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14453051</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ref11"><label>11</label><citation citation-type="journal">Kannel WB. Coronary heart disease risk factors in the elderly. <source>Am J Geriatr Cardiol</source><year>2002</year>;<volume>11</volume>:<fpage>101</fpage>-7.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11872968</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ref12"><label>12</label><citation citation-type="journal">Anderson KM, Wilson PWF, Odell PM, Kannel WB. An updated coronary risk profile - a statement for health-professionals. <source>Circulation</source><year>1991</year>;<volume>83</volume>:<fpage>356</fpage>-62.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1984895</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ref13"><label>13</label><citation citation-type="journal">Anderson KM, Odell PM, Wilson PWF, Kannel WB. Cardiovascular-disease risk profiles. <source>Am Heart J</source><year>1991</year>;<volume>121</volume>:<fpage>293</fpage>-8.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1985385</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ref14"><label>14</label><citation citation-type="journal">Kannel WB, D&#x02019;Agostino RB. The importance of cardiovascular risk factors in the elderly. <source>Am J Geriatr Cardiol</source><year>1995</year>;<volume>4</volume>:<fpage>10</fpage>-23.</citation></ref><ref id="ref15"><label>15</label><citation citation-type="journal">Bemmel T, Gussekloo J, Westendorp RG, Blauw GJ. In a population-based prospective study, no association between high blood pressure and mortality after age 85 years. <source>J Hypertens</source><year>2006</year>;<volume>24</volume>:<fpage>287</fpage>-92.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16508574</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ref16"><label>16</label><citation citation-type="journal">Boshuizen HC, Izaks GJ, van Buuren S, Ligthart GJ. Blood pressure and mortality in elderly people aged 85 and older: community based study. <source>BMJ</source><year>1998</year>;<volume>316</volume>:<fpage>1780</fpage>-4.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9624064</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ref17"><label>17</label><citation citation-type="journal">Oates DJ, Berlowitz DR, Glickman ME, Silliman RA, Borzecki AM. Blood pressure and survival in the oldest old. <source>J Am Geriatr Soc</source><year>2007</year>;<volume>55</volume>:<fpage>383</fpage>-8.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17341240</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ref18"><label>18</label><citation citation-type="journal">Rastas S, Pirttila T, Viramo P, Verkkoniemi A, Halonen P, Juva K, et al. Association between blood pressure and survival over 9 years in a general population aged 85 and older. <source>J Am Geriatr Soc</source><year>2006</year>;<volume>54</volume>:<fpage>912</fpage>-8.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16776785</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ref19"><label>19</label><citation citation-type="journal">Weverling-Rijnsburger AW, Blauw GJ, Lagaay AM, Knook DL, Meinders AE, Westendorp RG. Total cholesterol and risk of mortality in the oldest old. <source>Lancet</source><year>1997</year>;<volume>350</volume>:<fpage>1119</fpage>-23.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9343498</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ref20"><label>20</label><citation citation-type="journal">Abramson J, Wright JM. Are lipid-lowering guidelines evidence-based? <source>Lancet</source><year>2007</year>;<volume>369</volume>:<fpage>168</fpage>-9.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17240267</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ref21"><label>21</label><citation citation-type="journal">Ali R, Alexander KP. Statins for the primary prevention of cardiovascular events in older adults: a review of the evidence. <source>Am J Geriatr Pharmacother</source><year>2007</year>;<volume>5</volume>:<fpage>52</fpage>-63.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17608248</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ref22"><label>22</label><citation citation-type="journal">Chobanian AV. Isolated systolic hypertension in the elderly. <source>N Engl J Med</source><year>2007</year>;<volume>357</volume>:<fpage>789</fpage>-96.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17715411</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ref23"><label>23</label><citation citation-type="journal">Beckett NS, Peters R, Fletcher AE, Staessen JA, Liu L, Dumitrascu D, et al. Treatment of hypertension in patients 80 years of age or older. <source>N Engl J Med</source><year>2008</year>;<volume>358</volume>:<fpage>1887</fpage>-98.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18378519</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ref24"><label>24</label><citation citation-type="journal">Shepherd J, Blauw GJ, Murphy MB, Bollen ELEM, Buckley BM, Cobbe SM, et al. Pravastatin in elderly individuals at risk of vascular disease (PROSPER): a randomised controlled trial. <source>Lancet</source><year>2002</year>;<volume>360</volume>:<fpage>1623</fpage>-30.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12457784</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ref25"><label>25</label><citation citation-type="journal">Folsom AR, Chambless LE, Ballantyne CM, Coresh J, Heiss G, Wu KK, et al. An assessment of incremental coronary risk prediction using c-reactive protein and other novel risk markers: the atherosclerosis risk in communities study. <source>Arch Intern Med</source><year>2006</year>;<volume>166</volume>:<fpage>1368</fpage>-73.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16832001</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ref26"><label>26</label><citation citation-type="journal">Wang TJ, Gona P, Larson MG, Tofler GH, Levy D, Newton-Cheh C, et al. Multiple biomarkers for the prediction of first major cardiovascular events and death. <source>N Engl J Med</source><year>2006</year>;<volume>355</volume>:<fpage>2631</fpage>-9.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17182988</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ref27"><label>27</label><citation citation-type="journal">Rothenbacher D, Koenig W, Brenner H. Comparison of N-terminal pro-B-natriuretic peptide, C-reactive protein, and creatinine clearance for prognosis in patients with known coronary heart disease. <source>Arch Intern Med</source><year>2006</year>;<volume>1